    "sentence_translations": [
      "Epilogue",
      "",
      "",
      "“The Painted Skin” is a story written by Pu Songling during the Qing dynasty.",
      "This is the last thing he wrote in this story: “Obviously it was a demon, but he thought it was a beauty.",
      "Obviously it was said for his own good, but he thought it was said maliciously.",
      "It was because he liked that beautiful human skin, nothing more…”",
      "",
      "China has a saying that goes like this:",
      "“It’s easy to draw a tiger’s skin, but hard to draw its bones. We may know a person’s face, but not his heart.”",
      "This also means the same thing. It’s easy to draw a tiger, but hard to draw the bones of a tiger.",
      "Knowing people is very easy, but it is difficult to know their hearts.",
      "",
      "Some people think that when Pu Songling wrote “the beggar’s saliva turned into a human heart, ..",
      ".. and finally Wang Sheng came alive”, it was to tell everyone, ..",
      ".. that people like Wang Sheng have hearts like the spit of a beggar, both filthy and repulsive.",
      ""
    ]
